            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous healing of an osteochondroma fracture.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>283-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diii.2014.11.013</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S2211-5684(14)00313-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteochondroma is the most common benign tumor of bone, usually asymptomatic. Fracture of an osteochondroma is a rare complication and has been recognized as a cause of pain. Treatment of this fracture is controversial and some authors suggest fracture as an indication for surgical excision. We present a case of fractured osteochondroma that healed without complication.</AbstractText>
